WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.860
In the last episode, we had a bloody brutal fight against Ludwig.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.260
And at the start of that fight, do you remember this guy ?

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.460
He was the corpse that came towards us in the opening cutscene.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.760
Well, on my second fight with Ludwig on a new character,

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.480
I discovered that it's possible for this guy to survive the fight.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.620
He didn't get hit once as Ludwig stumped all over the place.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.440
Of course, all of my attempts, just think about how unlikely that is.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.800
He is probably laughing here like what the fuck how did i survive that ?

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.060
On my other character, this guy is dead, even during the fight with Ludwig that are still ongoing.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.840
So i guess you get one chance to save his life.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:46.760
And while i'm busy discovering all these pointless things, you guys are finding some really cool stuff

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.120
Commenter AKnaught92, in the last video, found something particularly awesome.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:58.360
If you talk to Ludwig's head after the boss fight, while wearing the garb of the Healing Church,

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.680
the he says this:

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.760
"Tell me, good hunter of the Church."

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.580
"Have you seen the light?"

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:12.700
"Are my Church Hunters the honorable spartans I hoped they would be?"

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.820
"Ah, good...that is a relief."

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:23.860
"To know I did not suffer such denigration for nothing."

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:30.780
"Thank you kindly. Now I may sleep in peace."

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:40.200
"Even in this darkest of nights, I see...the moonlight..."

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.820
I guess i didn't have the heart to tell him that his Church Hunters are now blood raving lunatics

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.760
I'll be checking out what happens if you say no here though

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.600
It should make for some pretty sad stuff for prepare to cry, right?

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.240
Telling him that his life's work was for nothing.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:02.560
But it turns out there is one blade of the Healing Church still alive and human in the nightmare.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.840
"Shrouded by night, but with steady stride."

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.860
"Coloured by blood, but always clear of mind."

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.300
"Proud hunter of the Church."

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.480
"Beasts are a curse, and a curse is a shackle."

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.240
"Only ye are the true blades of the church."

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:23.280
He's reciting some chant that the Healing Church Hunters must have learned

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.420
to keep themselves sane while hunting beasts

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.080
the repetition would have helped with anyone's sanity

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.560
and he's not the only one who does this

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:36.060
The next two characters we meet, in fact, have their own little chance going on.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.840
"Are you a hunter ?"

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.920
"Well, that's very odd."

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.400
"Do you hear the toll of the bell."

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:54.600
"Hmph. Liar. Such pettiness will be your undoing."

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.600
"The beasts you seek will not be found here."

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:04.980
Go back to your hunt, and if you have the chance, put this night behind you."

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:11.040
"...places better left untouched, secrets better left alone..."

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.100
"...only a fool would so brazenly roam..."

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.480
We're going to hearing that bell before too long,

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.540
and it turns out it's not a sound you want to hear.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.940
At the end of the hallway, we find the Fist of Gratia,

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:30.920
which belongs to this hulking brute of woman who didn't have the dexterity to wield firearms.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.780
And up ahead, we run into someone very familar

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.660
This is almost certainly Vicar Amelia, right ?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.680
It's the same chant we hear before her boss fight.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.340
The voice is the same, and it's her white garb.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:01.220
I'll be at less raggedy since this is based in the past, i think.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.000
We know that blood-crazed hunters ended up in the nightmare.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:08.540
So she must have ended up here when we put her to rest in the waking world.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:13.840
You have to kill Amelia in the waking world before you can access the DLC after all.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.000
As the eye pendant we found in the last video states,

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.600
this is the Cathedral of Healing Church that contains their the private research hall.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:28.760
The Church and the Choir have long experimented on patients in order to gain insight and

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.780
potentially ascend to the status of Great Ones

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:35.400
that much at least is clear from the law we learned so far

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.760
and this research hall can hopefully tell us a little more about

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.900
"Has someone, anyone, seen my eyes ?"

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.600
"I'm afraid i've dropped them in a puddle."

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:07.400
"Everything is pale, now..."

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.040
Is this Eileen?

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.320
Listen to the way she say puddle

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.260
"Puddle"

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.300
Sounds like when she says hunter

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.080
"Hunter"

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.120
The accent is the same, for sure, and maybe the voice as well.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:22.640
But beyond that, i guess we need a bit more proof.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.320
Anyway, the gameplay in this area is interesting,

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:31.340
for me, it was the closest series has come to having a stealth based level.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:34.220
I don't know if everyone else experienced this but i did.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:38.540
Because all throughout the level, you find these Blue Elixirs, which is a medicine

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.700
that used by high ministers of the Healing Church,

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:44.820
to numb the brains of those they experimented on

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:51.360
and they're certainly appropriate here in this research hall teeming with patients, with enlarged heads.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.720
Our character retains consciousness when they drink this through sheer force of will

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:01.040
And we make use of the secondary effect of the medicine, which is to go semi stealth

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.520
And I couldn't always be bothered killing every one of the patients

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.640
so often i would use blue elixir to scout out the level

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.660
and i had some pretty cool moments with it

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.240
Look at this guy run past

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:18.680
The Souls games are rare examples of games that actually reward you for being observant

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:22.440
some bookcases for example, have pressure plates in front of them

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.140
which when pressed trigger the bookcases to attack you

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.760
That's the sentence i never thought, I'd say

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.900
Also take for example, this huge winding stairway

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:36.000
some platforms you'll notice are inaccessible

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:39.100
which hints that staircase will rotate

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.920
later on and that you'll be rewarded for coming back and exploring again.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.700
I just really like stuff that rewards the observant player.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:53.300
And being observant really does reward you because the item you need here is the Loch Shield.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.080
A shield with such low requirements

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.980
that pretty much any build can be able to use it

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:04.280
It protects you against non physical damage and it's going to be really useful in the next boss fight.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:09.240
They've also done a really good job, i think of not just introducing new enemies

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.840
but variations on the same enemy.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:16.820
I can't say the same for games like Destiny that charge you $70.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:22.180
For an expansion with the same enemies and the enemies just have a different skin

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.200
No, in this game, there's tons of new enemies

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:32.740
and a lot of enemies like enlarged head patients, they all have vastly different movesets, meaning you're always guessing.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.060
Moving on a little bit, the main law question for this area is:

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:42.240
What was the Church hoping to archive with these patients ?

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.120
So, let's listen to some dialogue:

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:51.000
"Is that you, Lady Maria ? No, you're someone else ?"

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:55.460
"Please, could you do something to me?"

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:03.220
"I need Brain Fluid. Murky, mushy Brain Fluid..."

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:07.320
You find this Brain Fluid on fully developed heads,

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.020
the ones that talk about the sound that they're hearing.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.920
"Lady Maria, I'm a robin."

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.400
"Will I ever curl up and become a egg ?"

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:21.540
"What say you, Lady Maria ? Lady Maria ?"

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.980
"Say something, anything..."

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:29.300
"Have you heard how curiously the sea churns ?"

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:39.300
"Like the storm, but like the rain, only gentle, like dripping water..."

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:44.280
"It bellows, from deep inside of me..."

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:48.600
"Here it comes, up through my insides..."

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:52.520
"But gentle, like little droplets..."

00:08:55.420 --> 00:09:02.100
The Brain Fluid reads: extracted from a patient whose head expanded until that was all that they were.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.000
These heads and the patients that have them,

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.080
they're kind of insight experiments that you would expect from the Church.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:12.020
Clearly, the things they're saying have some significance

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.280
they're all related to water,

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.920
they're not just ramblings of insane people.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:22.320
The importance of large bodies of water is actually referenced in a lot of runes.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:30.060
The lake rune, for example, say that they  serve as a bulwark guarding sleep, and an augur of the eldritch Truth.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:36.560
They say that the transcription of the Great Ones' inhuman voices ripples like a watery reflection

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:41.460
They say that we must overcome the hindrance of water, and seek what is ours.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:45.380
And in the next video, we'll learn a bit more about what this means

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:50.060
but just know for now, that these beings clearly have more insight.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:57.480
Even though it's really specific, that these enlarge heads that hear the water and so will we, soon.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.920
One patient that hasn't completely turned into a large head,

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.100
talks about being a failure.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:08.680
As if she let down the Lady Maria, who all the patients clearly see as

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.960
some caring motherly figure.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:15.380
One character in particular talks the most, she's called Saint Adeline

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:19.640
and we help her take three helpings of brain fluid

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:20.940
and then

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:28.140
"Ahh! Ahhh! I see a shape."

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:36.720
"My guide, I see your voice, clearly, as it bends and bleeds."

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:47.500
"My own, revelation...just for me..."

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:53.100
"Thank you, for everything..."

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:57.000
"Really, I used to be nothing..."

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:11.980
She's so proud that she became something, like she finally had this purpose .

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.260
She gives you the Milkweed rune if you complete her quest,

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:16.860
which turns us into this thing.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.060
And also she gives us the Balcony Key,

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:25.200
which leads to the area that used to hold the celestial emissaries in the waking world.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:32.700
It's more proof that these patients were trying to be turned into kin, or these celestial emissaries.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:41.840
The Milkweed rune reads: A translation of the inhuman, sticky whispers that reveal the nature of a celestial attendant.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.000
Sounds a lot like a celestial emissary.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:49.060
Speaking of failure, this next boss, the Living Failure.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:53.900
To me, these things and by extension the other creatures in the research hall,

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:58.060
they all seem to be attempts at creating celestial in some form

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:00.540
and maybe even celestial emissaries

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:04.780
beings that can talks or communicate with the Great Ones perhaps.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.780
There are a lot of similarities, especially in regards to where you fight them.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:12.840
It's an interesting boss, every time you take one out, another one spawns

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.620
and there's always going to be four of them attacking you from all sides.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:20.440
They're incredibly slow but when you deplete their huge health pool,

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:23.920
they get bolder and more aggressive and more frantic.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:28.380
At around 50% heath, they start casting Meteor Storm together,

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:33.000
which is best defended against using the lock shield that we pick up earlier

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.620
as it defends against arcane projectiles.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:40.920
If you're well positioned, you can even get a backstab off while they cast the Meteor shower,

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:45.860
which I highly recommend because it's a way to get in that much needed damage.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:52.100
After succeeding, we talk to the wandering hunter.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:56.400
We're going to call him Simon for reasons I'll explain later.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:01.640
"Oh, hello. Not a pretty sight, is it?"

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:09.400
"The true face of the blood-worshipping, beast-purging Healing Church."

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.760
"But that’s not all."

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:17.200
"You seek the secrets field by the Nightmare, do you not?"

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.040
"Then here’s what you must do."

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:26.240
"Climb the Astral Clocktower, and kill Maria."

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:29.320
"She hides the real secret…"

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:50.500
"A corpse... should be left well alone."

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:07.000
"Oh, I know very well. How the secrets beckon so sweetly."

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:12.560
"Only an honest death will cure you now."

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:18.640
"Liberate you, from your wild curiosity."

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:26.980
Lady Maria, so far, all we know is that she's a caretaker of the patients in the clinic

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:29.280
and that she hides the true secrets.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:36.780
I am confident in saying that this was my favorite fight in Bloodborne so far.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:40.700
I love hunters boss fight in this game, because they put you on

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.580
what seems like even footing with an opponent

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:47.540
and it allows you to make good use of the health regain mechanic

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:51.760
unlike most beasts enemies that just flatten you in one or two hits.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:55.740
I hate that, i love when it's a fight where you can regain your health.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:15:00.040
You can probably parry her but I wasn't gonna find out,

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:04.400
I feel like spamming parry is a really shitty way to do this fight.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:09.260
I wanted to dash around and use my reflexes and my blades of mercy

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.700
and I just wanted to get through all of her phases that way

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:19.220
And as we're discovering every boss in the old hunters has phases, Lady Maria is no different.

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:20.660
She has three.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:24.240
Every time i fought her, i fought one stage further.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:27.800
I did this, because her phases are actually pretty well designed.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:34.560
It's not like fighting Ludwig, where you fight a completely different version of him at 50% of his health.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:42.240
No, Maria trains you in her attacks, every phases simply upgrades the attack that she's already been using.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:48.380
Meaning that earlier phases train you for future phases, and they reward you for learning.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:49.540
Such a good fight.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:55.580
And I'll tell you now, Maria is going to make a fantastic prepare to cry story.

00:15:55.580 --> 00:16:00.980
There is so much interesting stuff to talk about but we'll have to do it in another time.

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.560
Let's talk a little bit about it.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:08.060
So as her set says she's an apprentice to Gerhman, someone who looked up to him

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:12.580
though he has an affection for her that she didn't seem to sense.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:18.860
Since Gehrman modeled the Hunters Dream, it's clear that the doll is actually modeled after Maria.

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:22.800
This caretaker who shares most of physical attributes

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:27.540
Maria is a caretaker of the patients and the Doll is a caretaker of of us.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.460
There's a lot of similarities there, not just appearance.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:35.680
However, Gehrman certainly seems displeased with the Doll in the Dream.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:41.080
And for a man who is supposedly created the Doll out of love for another woman,

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.860
he never interacts with her.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:47.020
Perhaps it's because the Doll has a completely different personality.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:51.460
Maybe it's because she's far less headstrong and way more subservient,

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:54.920
he couldn't replicate who Maria was in the Dream

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:59.200
But, yeah, lots to talk about, i'll see you guys in the next one

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:03.460
Thank you for watching and it's time to get into some secrets.

